The exact decision object is the paper’s binary directional coverage matrix \(B\), budget \(k\), and threshold \(L=z\) (Corollary 1). Its witness is a projection subset, verified by matrix coverage in \(O(kz)\). I’m testing a theorem-licensed Set Cover/X3C regime with a planted exact cover: every planted and decoy projection covers exactly three directions, so plants have no per-row signature; the required standard attack is Algorithm X, not merely greedy.
